.TH QFW_GHZ.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_ghz.sh \- run a Qiskit or PennyLane GHZ test through QFw
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_ghz.sh [common-options] framework qubits backend iterations
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_ghz.sh
builds and executes a GHZ circuit with either Qiskit or PennyLane. It reserves
capacity for 1,024 shots per iteration, starts or connects to the requested
QPM, launches through
.BR qfw-srun (1),
and tears down application-owned runtime state.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I framework
Use
.B qiskit
or
.BR pennylane .
.TP
.I qubits
Positive circuit width.
.TP
.I backend
QPM provider name, such as
.BR nwqsim ,
.BR fake-iqm ,
or
.BR iqm .
An explicit
.B --backend
option takes precedence.
.TP
.I iterations
Positive number of circuit submissions.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-mode " mode"
Use application-owned
.B local
services or an existing
.B site
QPM. The default is local.
.TP
.BI --backend " name"
Override the positional backend.
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Override the activated site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Override the installed runtime selected by the service mode.
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing.
.PP
Common options must precede the positional arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run four Qiskit GHZ iterations on an application-owned NWQSim QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_ghz.sh --service-mode local \e
  qiskit 4 nwqsim 4
.EE
.PP
Run one two-qubit Qiskit circuit on a site-owned IQM QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_ghz.sh --service-mode site --backend iqm \e
  qiskit 2 iqm 1
.EE
